From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_hnat: preserve ppd_dev bridge FDB mark

When pseudo-port device ppd_dev ("hnat") is bridged under br-lan, HNAT
packets returning from PPE with VLAN 1234 (or non-force-CPU UNBIND frames
arriving directly on GMAC3) must retain skb->mark == 0x78681415 across
do_hnat_ext_to_ge2() and mtk_poll_rx() so br_handle_frame_finish() skips
br_fdb_update() instead of flooding "received packet on hnat with own
address as source address" and net_ratelimit warnings.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c           | 2 ++
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -2892,6 +2892,8 @@ static int mtk_poll_rx(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget,
 			skb->protocol = eth_hdr(skb)->h_proto;
 			skb->dev = ppd_dev;
 			skb->mark = 0x78681415;
+		} else if (ppd_dev && skb->dev == ppd_dev) {
+			skb->mark = 0x78681415;
 		}
 		skb_record_rx_queue(skb, 0);
 		napi_gro_receive(napi, skb);
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
@@ -1272,7 +1272,9 @@ unsigned int do_hnat_ext_to_ge2(struct sk_buff *skb, const char *func)
 				(skb_hnat_entry(skb) != 0x3fff))))
 			skb_set_hash(skb, skb_hnat_entry(skb) >> 1, PKT_HASH_TYPE_L4);
 
-		if (unlikely(skb->mark == 0x78681415))
+		if (dev == READ_ONCE(ppd_dev))
+			skb->mark = 0x78681415;
+		else if (unlikely(skb->mark == 0x78681415))
 			skb->mark = 0;
 
 		set_from_extge(skb);
